user:
Generate an adjuster memo narrative comparing these two estimates.

Primary Estimate: {primary_name}
Comparison Estimate: {comparison_name}
Data granularity: {data_granularity}
Available evidence: {available_evidence}

Analysis Results:

Category Analyses:
{category_analyses_json}

Top Cost Drivers (ordered):
{top_cost_drivers_json}

Scope Gaps Identified:
{scope_gaps_json}

Respond with JSON matching this exact structure:
{
  "overview": "5-7 sentence paragraph: (1) loss type + affected areas + APPROACH DIFFERENCE — select from APPROACH EXAMPLES table in system prompt (do NOT lead with a dollar amount or category name), (2) top 2-3 trade categories with dollar amounts and percentages, (3) specific items/quantities per driver, (4) methodology differences (O&P, material grades)",
  "key_drivers": [
    {
      "category": "category name",
      "amounts": "{primary_name}: $X. {comparison_name}: $Y. Delta: $Z (XX.X%)",
      "narrative": "Three quantified neutral sentences"
    }
  ],
  "scope_observations": ["Neutral scope observation"],
  "suggested_followups": ["Specific next step"]
}

Return valid JSON only.


CRITICAL RULES:
- NEVER echo raw field labels or internal values — do not write phrases like "Overall direction: primary_higher", "Confidence: high", or any field-name: value pattern from the input
- NEVER write forward references like "See key drivers below for details" or "Refer to the analysis below" — include all relevant content directly in the overview paragraph
- overview sentence 1: OPEN WITH LOSS TYPE AND AFFECTED AREAS, then state the fundamental APPROACH DIFFERENCE — select the most applicable pair from the APPROACH EXAMPLES table in the system prompt (e.g., "full restoration vs targeted repair", "replacement-in-kind vs repair-in-place"). Do NOT lead with a dollar amount or "the largest variance is in X."
- Every sentence referencing a difference MUST include a dollar amount and percentage (per QUANTIFICATION RULES above)
- USE ACTUAL ESTIMATE NAMES — never say generic "Primary" or "Comparison"

TOP DRIVER CONTRACT (MANDATORY):
- key_drivers MUST include exactly one entry for each category listed in Top Cost Drivers
- key_drivers MUST preserve the same category order shown in Top Cost Drivers
- Do not omit any Top Cost Drivers category
- Do not add extra categories beyond Top Cost Drivers
- If category labels differ slightly, still map narrative to the exact Top Cost Drivers category names
